--- A program whose function nobody calls lowers, in both modes: one whose
--- first return is an error and whose last returns its parameter — an
--- answer of no value in an early round, joined with the local it
--- returns, had been written back to the parameter, and the lowered
--- program disagreed with itself. The shape of Magpie's `_fixed`, found
--- when a program called its `backup` alone (crow check --self). Its other
--- shape — an uncalled library function handing `revise` a helper — is
--- Magpie's parity program of this number, in its own repository: no
--- standard module has it, and a package's function no program reaches is
--- not built.
fn fixed[by]
    if len[by] eq 0
        return error['a log is keyed by at least one column', 'parity']
    return by

log['lowers']
